Israel bombed Gaza hospital after foreign medics were ordered out: Volunteer doctor
An international volunteer doctor at the Nasser Hospital in southern Gaza has confirmed that she and her foreign colleagues were made to leave the medical complex shortly before Israeli strikes killed about two dozen people, including five journalists, there.
@PressTV

Gaza urges global action nearly a year after abduction of hospital director
Gaza's Ministry of Health has called on the international community to address the case of Dr. Hussam Abu Safiya, the director of the Kamal Adwan Hospital, to expend efforts to uncover his whereabouts and work toward his release, as the first anniversary of his abduction by Israeli forces draws near.
@PressTV
